-- N,N-dimethylformamide, where the bond graph's count is right at one temperature and wrong at another.
-- Atoms: 0 the carbonyl carbon, 1 its oxygen, 2 the formyl hydrogen, 3 the nitrogen, 4 one methyl carbon
-- with hydrogens 5 to 7, 8 the other with hydrogens 9 to 11. The amide C-N bond has partial double-bond
-- character, so the nitrogen and its two methyls lie in the carbonyl's plane and the two methyls are not
-- the same: one is cis to the oxygen and one is trans. Nothing about the connectivity says so -- in the
-- bond graph they are exchanged by an automorphism -- and nothing about handedness either, since the
-- molecule is planar and achiral. What separates them is that the motion which would exchange them,
-- rotation about the C-N bond, is slow: the free energy of activation is 19 to 21 kcal/mol in solution,
-- 21.0 by total line-shape analysis in carbon tetrachloride, which by the Eyring relation is a rate of
-- about 10^-3 per second at room temperature and about 30 per second at 400 K.
dmf-obs : List Nat
dmf-obs = cons 2 (cons 5 (cons 6 (cons 7 (cons 9 (cons 10 (cons 11 nil))))))
